# AGL Pallet — Cursor rules (REDESIGN)
# Plan: docs/02-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md. Audit: docs/01-TECHNICAL-AUDIT.md.
# Do not read archive/ unless told to.

## Stack (do not re-derive)
- Next.js App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind v4 (tokens in app/globals.css @theme).
  If package.json still shows Next 14 / Tailwind 3, Phase 0 (R0.5) is not done yet.
- UI sources, in priority order: shadcn/ui core → Magic UI → ReUI → Aceternity (nav only).
  Animation: motion/react only. No GSAP, no Lenis, no other registries without approval.
- Icons: lucide-react only.
- Class merging: `import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"` only.
- Images: next/image. Video: native <video>, never a player library for background loops.
- trailingSlash: true — internal links end with a slash (/products/).
- Package name nx7k-lab-m4 matches Vercel. Don't rename.

## Content rules (compliance — unchanged)
- Owner decisions D1–D6 in docs/01-TECHNICAL-AUDIT.md §8 are approved and override
  older rules in BRIEF.md/PROJECT.md where they conflict (incl. BRIEF §H3 on form services).
- Copy lives in content/**.json. Never hardcode copy in components. Never edit content
  JSON during a design task; flag copy problems in a comment instead.
- Body copy is verbatim from SPEC_V1.md. Changing heading CASE for presentation is allowed;
  changing heading WORDS is not.
- AGL is a pallet BROKERAGE, never a manufacturer. Never write make/produce/build/manufacture/
  our mill/our plant/our factory with AGL as subject.
- Banned everywhere (including alt, meta, JSON-LD): warehousing/storage/inventory/VMI;
  certification claims; recycled/used pallets; customer/supplier/competitor names; any
  number not in SPEC_V1; "national"/"nationwide"; exclamation points; emoji.
- {{TBD-*}} tokens render visibly. Never fill them with invented content.
- Never change routes, H1 text, canonicals, or JSON-LD output.

## Design rules (NEW — these replace the old port rules)
- Palette 05 "Premium Dark" ONLY: moss #131913, green #1F2A1F, smoke #2E342F,
  gray #AEB5AE, bone #ECE8DF, ice #DDE9E2. No other colors, no hue accent (no orange/amber).
  Emphasis = ice, weight, scale, photography.
- Marketing pages lead dark (moss ground, green inset cards, smoke surfaces, bone text).
  Reading pages (articles, glossary, calculators, forms) use bone grounds with moss text.
- Palette 03 tokens (parchment, cream, fog, mint, clay, cocoa, ink) are retired. Don't use them.
- Radius: inputs 10px, cards 18px, section containers 28px, buttons full pill.
  No square corners on cards, images, inputs, tables, menus, or sections.
- Dark sections are rounded INSET cards with margin, not full-bleed slabs.
  Full-bleed is allowed only for the home video hero and photo bands.
- Type: Anton (font-display) ONLY for hero H1s and `.display`. Everything else Inter,
  sentence case. Uppercase only for small eyebrows. Body 16px.
- Buttons: `primary` (dark pill) and `secondary` (outline pill), optional arrow. Nothing else.
- Cards are allowed for features, resources, steps, and choices. Use gaps, soft shadows,
  and hover lift — not thick borders.
- Vary page openers (see R4.1). Don't stack identical dark heroes.
- Body measure max 70ch, text-wrap: balance on headings, 16px min gutter,
  no horizontal scroll at 375px.

## Motion rules
- Every animated component: "use client", lazy below the fold, respects
  prefers-reduced-motion (render static), causes no layout shift.
- Reveals: use the shared <Reveal> (Magic UI Blur Fade). Animate sections, not every element.
- Border Beam: primary hero CTA only. No particles, cursor effects, or gooey tabs.

## How to work
- This project runs on a fast, low-cost model by default. Stay inside the task: no refactors,
  no "while I'm here" edits, no rereading large docs you don't need.
- If the build still fails after your second fix attempt, or you can't meet the task's
  "Done when", STOP. Report what you tried, the exact error, and your best guess at the cause.
  Don't keep looping; the owner will rerun the task on a stronger model.
- One task ID per chat (e.g. R2.1). Touch only the files the task needs.
- Install registry components via the CLI; adapt them, don't rewrite from scratch.
- Before finishing: `npm run build`. Before merging a phase: `npm run verify`.
- Gates: CLS < 0.05, LCP < 2.5s, mobile Lighthouse Perf ≥ 95, zero serious/critical axe,
  schema/routes/banned-words/numbers green. Never soften a gate without written approval.
- Commit message starts with the task ID. One driver (Cursor or Claude Code) at a time.
- Deviations → DECISIONS.md. Blockers → BLOCKED.md. Durable state → PROGRESS.md (keep short).
- Push to main → Vercel builds. Never touch DNS or the live WordPress site.
